Read the screen with `describe` before and after to see where focus landed.
Returns { pressed, count }. Fails on a target that is not a TV, and on the Apple TV simulator for rewind, fastForward, next, previous, volumeUp, volumeDown and mute (its HID stack ignores them); every other button works on all three platforms.","signature":"tools.argent["tv-remote"]({
  /** Target TV device id from `list-devices` (Apple TV, Android TV, or Vega). */
  udid: string,
  /**
   * A single TV-remote button, or a path of them run in one call. Move focus with up/down/left/right, confirm with select, go back with back/menu, exit with home; the media and volume buttons press the matching remote keys. For multi-step navigation pass an array, e.g. ["up","right","right","select"]; strongly prefer this over multiple `tv-remote` calls: the whole path runs in a single call. Max items: 64.
   */
  button: "up" | "down" | "left" | "right" | "select" | "back" | "home" | "menu" | "playPause" | "rewind" | "fastForward" | "next" | "previous" | "volumeUp" | "volumeDown" | "mute" | Array<"up" | "down" | "left" | "right" | "select" | "back" | "home" | "menu" | "playPause" | "rewind" | "fastForward" | "next" | "previous" | "volumeUp" | "volumeDown" | "mute">,
  /**
   * Repeat the whole `button` value this many times (default 1). Compact for long same-button runs, e.g. { button: "down", repeat: 12 }. Range: 1 to 50.
   * @integer @minimum 1 @maximum 50
   */
  repeat?: number,
}): Promise<unknown>"},{"path":"tools.argent["gesture-pinch"]","description":"Execute a pinch-to-zoom gesture by moving two fingers toward or away from a center point to change the scale of on-screen content. Positions and distances are fractions of the screen (0.0–1.0, not pixels), as in gesture-tap.
startDistance > endDistance = pinch in (zoom out). startDistance < endDistance = pinch out (zoom in).
Typical values: startDistance 0.2, endDistance 0.6 for a zoom-in pinch at screen center.
Use when you need to zoom in or out on a map, image, or zoomable view. Returns { pinched: true, timestampMs }. On physical iOS, reactivated: true = app was re-fronted; re-describe. Fails if the simulator-server / emulator backend is not reachable for the given device, or on a physical iPhone when the app is not drawn in portrait.","signature":"tools.argent["gesture-pinch"]({
  /** Target device id from `list-devices` (iOS UDID or Android serial). */
  udid: string,
  /** Center of the pinch, horizontal. */
  centerX: number,
  /** Center of the pinch, vertical. */
  centerY: number,
  /** Initial distance between the two fingers. */
  startDistance: number,
  /** Final distance between the two fingers. */
  endDistance: number,
  /**
   * Final horizontal center of the pinch. When set, the centroid drifts linearly from centerX to endCenterX over the gesture (e.g. to keep expanding fingers on-screen near an edge). Omit for a fixed center.
   */
  endCenterX?: number,
  /** Final vertical center of the pinch; drifts from centerY like endCenterX. Omit for a fixed center. */
  endCenterY?: number,
  /** Angle in degrees of the axis the fingers lie on: 0 = horizontal (default), 90 = vertical. */
  angle?: number,
  /** Total gesture duration in milliseconds (default 300) */
  durationMs?: number,
}): Promise<unknown>"},{"path":"tools.argent["chromium-tabs"]","description":"List and switch the tabs / windows of a Chromium (CDP) app (an Electron app's BrowserWindows or a Chromium browser's tabs), and open or close them.
The active tab is what describe / gesture-tap / screenshot / debugger-evaluate / open-url all operate on, so select a tab before driving it. tabIds (`t1`, `t2`, …) are stable for the session and never reused.
Use when an app exposes multiple windows or tabs and you need to inspect or drive one other than the current page, or to open/close a page during an e2e test.
Returns { tabs: [{ tabId, targetId, title, url, active, label? }] } after the action. Fails if the device is not a Chromium (CDP) device, or the requested tabId/label no longer matches a live tab.","signature":"tools.argent["chromium-tabs"]({
  /** Chromium device id from `list-devices` (e.g. `chromium-cdp-9222`). */
  udid: string,
  /**
   * list: enumerate tabs/windows. select: make a tab active. new: open a tab and activate it. close: close a tab; if it was active, another live tab becomes active.
   */
  action: "list" | "select" | "new" | "close",
  /** Target tab for `select` (required) / `close`: a tabId like `t2` or a label. `close` defaults to the active tab. */
  tab?: string,
  /** `new` only: URL to open (defaults to about:blank). */
  url?: string,
  /** `new` only: a memorable label usable interchangeably with the tabId. */
  label?: string,
}): Promise<unknown>"},{"path":"tools.argent["menu-bar"]","description":"Read and choose the menu bar commands of a Mac app (File > Export..., Edit > Select All). The menu bar is outside the app window: describe does not show it, and gesture-tap cannot reach it.
Use when a command lives in the app's menus. Use keyboard instead for a shortcut you already know, and file-panel for the open or save panel that a command shows.
list returns { menuBar }, one line per item indented under its menu: the title (a menu ends with " >"), [disabled] or [checked], the shortcut in keyboard syntax, and id="..." when the item has one. choose takes path (the titles from the menu bar down, e.g. ["File", "Export..."]) or identifier, and returns { chosen } with the path; the command runs right after the reply.
Fails if no item matches (the error lists the titles at that level), if the item is disabled or is a menu, if a menu of the app is open, or if the device is not a Mac app.","signature":"tools.argent["menu-bar"]({
  /** Mac app id from `list-devices` (macos-app-<bundle id>). */
  udid: string,
  /** list: the app's menu bar, one line per item. choose: run one menu item, by path or identifier. */
  action: "list" | "choose",
  /**
   * For choose: the titles from the menu bar down to the item, as list shows them, e.g. ["File", "Export..."]. Case and "..." versus "…" do not matter. Max items: 9.
   * @minItems 1 @maxItems 9
   * Each item: @minLength 1
   */
  path?: Array<string>,
  /** For choose: the item's id="..." from list, instead of path. @minLength 1 */
  identifier?: string,
}): Promise<unknown>"}],"remaining":60,"next":{"offset":10}}

